    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a difficult schedule today with the majority of the active roster enjoying an off-day, limiting our starting options to just three players. **Trea Turner** (65.16) and **Kyle Schwarber** (62.24) represent our strongest plays against Christian Scott. Both are projected for strong starts despite the 31% rain risk in New York. **Trea Turner**\u2019s value is bolstered by his assumed leadoff status, adding a 10% premium to his base score, which is critical given our league\u2019s aggressive pursuit of stolen bases. **Kyle Schwarber** continues to be a high-upside play, benefiting from an elite .377 xwOBA that keeps his ceiling elevated even against a competent arm like Scott. \n\n**Carson Benge** (51.45) rounds out our lineup in the utility slot, earning a marginal start. While he faces a tough challenge against Aaron Nola, his platoon advantage provides enough of a statistical cushion to justify his insertion. Unfortunately, our depth is neutralized by team off-days for heavy hitters like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Christian Yelich**. With the remainder of our roster\u2014including **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014all inactive today, we are effectively playing a short-handed roster. The primary risk remains the weather; should the rain in New York intensify and lead to a postponement, our daily cap efficiency will plummet. We will monitor the lineup cards closely for **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Carson Benge** to ensure no late-scratch defensive rests occur.",
